# 00-common-git-commit-message-rule.mdc - Git Commit Message Rules

## Scope

- MUST apply this rule when automatically generating Git commit messages.

## Language and Style

- MUST write commit messages in Japanese.
- MUST keep commit messages as short and concise as possible.
- MUST use bullet points in the body.
- MUST separate the title and body with one blank line.

## Required Format

- MUST split the message into a title and body.
- MUST use this structure:

```text
<TITLE>

<BODY>
```

- MUST write the body as bullet points, for example:

```text
TSVエクスポートとセル加工ロジックの追加。その他1件。

- TSVエクスポート機能を改善し、2行目のデータを追加。
- 空行をスキップする処理を実装し、セルの値を適切に加工するロジックを追加。
- 新しいsetup関数を作成し、初期設定完了時のアラート表示とボタン削除機能を実装。
```

## Content Rules

- MUST use the title to summarize the main change.
- SHOULD include `その他N件` in the title when there are additional meaningful changes.
- MUST keep the title concise.
- SHOULD describe the change and its purpose rather than listing only edited files.
- MUST NOT create an overly long title that repeats every body bullet.
